## Why the search is converged
The op is `C = A @ B.T`, fp16, N=K=4096, M small/variable — it is HBM-bandwidth bound on reading
B (33.55 MB) once. cuBLAS/`torch.matmul` (the reference) already runs this as a single fused,
hardware-tuned skinny-GEMM kernel at ~735 GB/s (45–70 µs). Every structural lever available to a
Triton kernel on sm_80 has now been tested and none closes the gap:

1. **Plain single-pass NT GEMM — swept to a hard ~0.58x ceiling.**
   - c001 0.56x (baseline), c004 0.56x (wider autotune / L2 grouping), c005 0.57x (coalesced
     [N,K] B load + tl.trans + wide BLOCK_K), c007 **0.58x** (the untested corner: full occupancy
     BLOCK_N=32→128 blocks *and* wide BLOCK_K=128/256 *and* deep cp.async stages, together).
   - Occupancy, burst width, pipeline depth, coalescing, and tiling are all exhausted; the surface
     is flat at ~0.58x (successive ideas each < 2% — inside timing noise).

2. **Split-K (the main draft hypothesis, H3) — both reduction strategies lose.**
   - c002 invalid (autotune atomic-without-reset overflow), c003 fixed atomic split-K **0.38x**,
     c006 deterministic two-pass fp32 reduction **0.49x**. At these ~50–100 µs latencies the extra
     kernel launch + partial-buffer write/read (or atomic contention) costs more than the
     occupancy it buys. Falsifies H3/H4 for this workload class.

3. **Non-MMA GEMV streaming for tiny M (H8) — catastrophic.**
   - c008 M≤8 GEMV kernel: **0.40x** geomean, M=4 collapses to 0.09x (461 µs vs c007's 74 µs, ~6×
     slower) because the broadcast-outer-product runs the K-reduction on the vector/CUDA-core
     datapath with no ldmatrix/tensor-core pipeline and exposes B-load latency. Falsifies H8; the
     tl.dot MMA path (even padding 4→16 rows) is the better use of Ampere for tiny M.

## Irreducible gap
For these skinny shapes the reference is a single fused cuBLAS kernel with negligible launch and
pipeline-fill overhead and hardware skinny-GEMM scheduling. A Triton kernel on sm_80 pays
per-launch + pipeline-fill cost that is a large fraction of a 45–70 µs runtime, and cannot be
recovered by K-partitioning (adds a pass) or by dropping tensor cores (loses the MMA datapath).
No remaining structural idea offers headroom, so further evaluations would not improve the metric.

